[[:db/retract 17592186240618 :answer-field/choices 17592186239335] [:db/retract 17592186240618 :answer-field/choices 17592186240073] [:db/retract 17592186240618 :answer-field/choices 17592186238653] [:db/retract 17592186240618 :answer-field/choices 17592186238861] [:db/retract 17592186240618 :answer-field/choices 17592186238831] {:db/id 17592186115355 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6d6379e5-5dfa-520a-ae85-5ee99eafe5a8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6d6379e5-5dfa-520a-ae85-5ee99eafe5a8" :question/id #uuid "6d6379e5-5dfa-520a-ae85-5ee99eafe5a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-162655" :question/problem "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-t),\\,3,\\,\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2}⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,0).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $3$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/39/39266e152f7a52ee6cf56ad872704a110765e22c5d3fcea6f4b4c7565276ee24.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a8f3c7fa-d0ee-5ec1-aa68-12f5aac82ca4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a8f3c7fa-d0ee-5ec1-aa68-12f5aac82ca4" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8f3c7fa-d0ee-5ec1-aa68-12f5aac82ca4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8972d48e-41d2-5611-92db-f9c29b7de45d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8972d48e-41d2-5611-92db-f9c29b7de45d" "answer-e8ef6ccf-95c6-56c8-af3b-01ccd8f18aa2" "answer-c4aa47c9-6cf7-51d6-b801-5bc91a5fc512" "answer-2b564ded-2d25-5252-a530-06b94ce11880" "answer-fc681ce4-d810-5c12-bf19-bf52552bebbd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8972d48e-41d2-5611-92db-f9c29b7de45d" :answer/id #uuid "8972d48e-41d2-5611-92db-f9c29b7de45d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-\\infty ,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8ef6ccf-95c6-56c8-af3b-01ccd8f18aa2" :answer/id #uuid "e8ef6ccf-95c6-56c8-af3b-01ccd8f18aa2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-\\infty ,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4aa47c9-6cf7-51d6-b801-5bc91a5fc512" :answer/id #uuid "c4aa47c9-6cf7-51d6-b801-5bc91a5fc512" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (0,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b564ded-2d25-5252-a530-06b94ce11880" :answer/id #uuid "2b564ded-2d25-5252-a530-06b94ce11880" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (0,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc681ce4-d810-5c12-bf19-bf52552bebbd" :answer/id #uuid "fc681ce4-d810-5c12-bf19-bf52552bebbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (3,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054631 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-751ef612-b871-5a13-b5db-9f9345197dd4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-751ef612-b871-5a13-b5db-9f9345197dd4" :question/id #uuid "751ef612-b871-5a13-b5db-9f9345197dd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-80813" :question/problem "Which of the following are subsets of ${Q}_{0}^{+}$ (the set of non-negative rational numbers)?\n\nI. ${Z}^{-}$ (the set of negative integers)\n\nII. $N$\n\nIII. ${Z}_{0}^{+}$ (the set of non-negative integers)" :question/worked-solution "$A$ is a subset of $B$ if every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect the given choices.\n\n- ${Z}^{-}$ is not a subset of ${Q}_{0}^{+}.$ For example, $-1\\in {Z}^{-}$ but $-1\\notin {Q}_{0}^{+}.$\n\n- $N$ is a subset of ${Q}^{+}.$ Indeed, every natural number is also a positive rational number.\n\n- ${Z}_{0}^{+}$ is a subset of ${Q}_{0}^{+}.$ Indeed, every positive integer is also a positive rational number. Notice also that  $0$ is in both  ${Z}_{0}^{+}$ and ${Q}_{0}^{+}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III  only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eb49e450-3c82-56fd-b065-47510e61dd32"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eb49e450-3c82-56fd-b065-47510e61dd32" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb49e450-3c82-56fd-b065-47510e61dd32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5ecaf329-877a-5184-b3cf-13e81c99934a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6bdcc3ed-d3b8-5907-ba40-01803c02c9cb" "answer-73df3086-3d04-5a6a-abd1-f9c01e475b78" "answer-ccc703f5-adf8-5933-89b8-12fe5ea4b4ee" "answer-5ecaf329-877a-5184-b3cf-13e81c99934a" "answer-c250bb51-b7ca-503c-842d-002259888993"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bdcc3ed-d3b8-5907-ba40-01803c02c9cb" :answer/id #uuid "6bdcc3ed-d3b8-5907-ba40-01803c02c9cb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73df3086-3d04-5a6a-abd1-f9c01e475b78" :answer/id #uuid "73df3086-3d04-5a6a-abd1-f9c01e475b78" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ccc703f5-adf8-5933-89b8-12fe5ea4b4ee" :answer/id #uuid "ccc703f5-adf8-5933-89b8-12fe5ea4b4ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ecaf329-877a-5184-b3cf-13e81c99934a" :answer/id #uuid "5ecaf329-877a-5184-b3cf-13e81c99934a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c250bb51-b7ca-503c-842d-002259888993" :answer/id #uuid "c250bb51-b7ca-503c-842d-002259888993" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162056 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d437ae95-9320-5f38-963e-97e760ec1b57"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d437ae95-9320-5f38-963e-97e760ec1b57" :question/id #uuid "d437ae95-9320-5f38-963e-97e760ec1b57" :question/math-academy-id "q-129384" :question/problem "Calculate $\\text{Var}[{2}^{k}]$ where $k$ is a constant." :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[a]=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[{2}^{k}]=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-acc41c54-687c-5d89-a864-5e4fafdd6f79"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-acc41c54-687c-5d89-a864-5e4fafdd6f79" :answer-field/id #uuid "acc41c54-687c-5d89-a864-5e4fafdd6f79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-608e3def-5a47-5698-9d7c-8d83b91fa89d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-608e3def-5a47-5698-9d7c-8d83b91fa89d" "answer-43972e47-c74a-5e2c-9406-cab735613c2d" "answer-e7b5533f-c67d-5f63-858e-8153fcb2ff84" "answer-040f7834-f2bb-5ae7-8210-05603a349336" "answer-d760d291-db5c-53dc-aa0b-1513d577346d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-608e3def-5a47-5698-9d7c-8d83b91fa89d" :answer/id #uuid "608e3def-5a47-5698-9d7c-8d83b91fa89d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43972e47-c74a-5e2c-9406-cab735613c2d" :answer/id #uuid "43972e47-c74a-5e2c-9406-cab735613c2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7b5533f-c67d-5f63-858e-8153fcb2ff84" :answer/id #uuid "e7b5533f-c67d-5f63-858e-8153fcb2ff84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-040f7834-f2bb-5ae7-8210-05603a349336" :answer/id #uuid "040f7834-f2bb-5ae7-8210-05603a349336" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d760d291-db5c-53dc-aa0b-1513d577346d" :answer/id #uuid "d760d291-db5c-53dc-aa0b-1513d577346d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2}^{k}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186241013 :question/problem "If $A=\\{1,2,4,8,16\\}$ and $B=\\{2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16\\},$ then $B∖A=$" :question/worked-solution "The set $B∖A$ is the set of all elements belonging to $B$ but *not* $A.$ Note that the elements $2,4,8,16\\in A$ are also in $B,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B∖A & =B-A \\\\  & =\\{2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16\\}-\\{1,2,4,8,16\\} \\\\  & =\\{6,10,12,14\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186240618 :answer-field/correct "answer-d162144b-b4a5-51ba-9d97-5bb11fc0f3da" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fb4e1fb8-de8c-57db-9ec1-0460004b76fc" "answer-bd06c2c2-b428-571e-8760-4cbeaa7dcc7a" "answer-d89d63a8-9075-5e20-bc27-e5a349ddda2d" "answer-d162144b-b4a5-51ba-9d97-5bb11fc0f3da" "answer-814bed9d-2cbb-5df1-896f-d87d4713951f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb4e1fb8-de8c-57db-9ec1-0460004b76fc" :answer/id #uuid "fb4e1fb8-de8c-57db-9ec1-0460004b76fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{1,16\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd06c2c2-b428-571e-8760-4cbeaa7dcc7a" :answer/id #uuid "bd06c2c2-b428-571e-8760-4cbeaa7dcc7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d89d63a8-9075-5e20-bc27-e5a349ddda2d" :answer/id #uuid "d89d63a8-9075-5e20-bc27-e5a349ddda2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{2,4,8,16\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d162144b-b4a5-51ba-9d97-5bb11fc0f3da" :answer/id #uuid "d162144b-b4a5-51ba-9d97-5bb11fc0f3da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{6,10,12,14\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-814bed9d-2cbb-5df1-896f-d87d4713951f" :answer/id #uuid "814bed9d-2cbb-5df1-896f-d87d4713951f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{6,12\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186362318 :question/problem "![](images/6b/6b9b15bd3c8cda84156d5461fb9f80f892a1dba26151cc37d381757f9f659fa1.png)\n\nConsider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y)$ where the graph of $f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $y=-3$ is a node.\n\nII. $y=2$ is a sink.\n\nIII. $y=2$ is a source." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083393 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-856c86c0-9a1d-541f-bee9-93df07ee1d90"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-856c86c0-9a1d-541f-bee9-93df07ee1d90" :question/id #uuid "856c86c0-9a1d-541f-bee9-93df07ee1d90" :question/math-academy-id "q-102697" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=6t-2$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=-1\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=1\\,\\text{s}$, calculate the speed of the particle at the moment $t=3\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (6t-2)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-2t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)=-1.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =3(1)^{2}-2(1)+C \\\\ -1 & =3-2+C \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=3{t}^{2}-2t-2.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=3\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =3(3)^{2}-2(3)-2 \\\\  & =27-6-2 \\\\  & =19\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $19\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ba55cb3c-40db-5e24-bdf4-2cb74a217cfc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ba55cb3c-40db-5e24-bdf4-2cb74a217cfc" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba55cb3c-40db-5e24-bdf4-2cb74a217cfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0de2057b-88f3-5eae-a4be-76fa3eb87360" :answer-field/choices ["answer-12fdb718-5b20-5e1f-bedc-4a924bf08daa" "answer-df95a53e-89cb-595f-b895-96655799381a" "answer-28abf313-cb2f-5450-b131-e9fc73d1c015" "answer-0de2057b-88f3-5eae-a4be-76fa3eb87360" "answer-d2363bc7-c793-5cae-a7a0-fdb45b1f9144"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12fdb718-5b20-5e1f-bedc-4a924bf08daa" :answer/id #uuid "12fdb718-5b20-5e1f-bedc-4a924bf08daa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df95a53e-89cb-595f-b895-96655799381a" :answer/id #uuid "df95a53e-89cb-595f-b895-96655799381a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28abf313-cb2f-5450-b131-e9fc73d1c015" :answer/id #uuid "28abf313-cb2f-5450-b131-e9fc73d1c015" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0de2057b-88f3-5eae-a4be-76fa3eb87360" :answer/id #uuid "0de2057b-88f3-5eae-a4be-76fa3eb87360" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2363bc7-c793-5cae-a7a0-fdb45b1f9144" :answer/id #uuid "d2363bc7-c793-5cae-a7a0-fdb45b1f9144" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186241023 :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s-4t=1 \\\\ -2s+5t=1 \\\\ -s-t=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s-4t=1 \\\\ t=-1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-4t & =1 \\\\ s-4(-1) & =1 \\\\ s+4 & =1 \\\\ s & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-3,\\,t=-1,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-3b-c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-3)\\cdot (-1)=3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186338872 :question/problem "Consider the straight line with the parametric equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2+4t \\\\ y=-3+5t \\\\ z=7-6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-6cb09053-a488-5c02-964c-0f5928dc5b08" :activity/id #uuid "6cb09053-a488-5c02-964c-0f5928dc5b08" :activity/title "Quiz 8" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-ca3a1e0a-5bd3-54a7-beb6-fad92e68d746" "step-6ecb1c55-62bb-540c-82e8-c73c10ae3111" "step-c44e9c92-4a17-5e6c-8c86-3e098f699c9a" "step-fe9c8f97-341d-5c62-9860-e88ab777c5b4" "step-11e9ef78-3c1d-5304-92fe-98c32e4f645a" "step-67d9c9df-eb88-5700-a91b-21973dca0f26" "step-2e9b0e94-e8c8-557f-b348-b08f